# What kills the most people?
subtitle: "Rank five of the world's biggest killers, then see why the heart, the blood vessels and the lungs top the list."

## What kills the most people?
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Heart disease
      - Stroke
      - COPD
      - Lung infections
      - Diabetes
    values:
      - 9.1
      - 7
      - 3.5
      - 2.5
      - 1.6
    bar_colors: same
    y_label: Deaths a year, millions
    icons:
      - anatomical heart
      - brain
      - lungs
      - microbe
      - syringe
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 11
sources:
    - id: who
      title: The top 10 causes of death (fact sheet, 2021 data)
      authors: World Health Organization
      year: 2024
      url: https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/the-top-10-causes-of-death
      finding: 'of 68 million deaths in 2021: ischaemic heart disease 9.1 million (13 %), stroke about 10 %, COPD about 5 %, lower respiratory infections 2.5 million, diabetes 1.6 million'

    cards kill cites ["who"] ends ["most","fewest"] hidden true
        * "Heart disease" icon "anatomical heart"
        * "Stroke" icon brain
        * "COPD" icon lungs
        * "Lung infections" icon microbe
        * "Diabetes" icon syringe
    text n1 "9.1 M" x 200 y 612 font_size 30 hidden true
    text n2 "7.0 M" x 362 y 511 font_size 30 hidden true
    text n3 "3.5 M" x 524 y 344 font_size 30 hidden true
    text n4 "2.5 M" x 686 y 296 font_size 30 hidden true
    text n5 "1.6 M" x 848 y 253 font_size 30 hidden true

What kills the most people in the world? Here are five of the biggest killers, in no particular order.
    draw kill

    ask "Put them in order, the one that kills the most first." on kill store k tolerance 0.2
        right: {k} in place.
        wrong: {k} in place.

    erase kill

Now count the deaths. Heart disease leads, at about nine million a year.
    draw axes bar_1 n1

Stroke follows, at seven million.
    draw bar_2 n2

Both are diseases of the blood vessels, and together they cause nearly one death in four.
    text quarter "≈ 1 in 4 deaths" #b5482e cites ["who"] x 470 y 650 font_size 32

Next come the lungs: COPD, mostly from tobacco and smoky indoor air, and then pneumonia and other lung infections.
    draw bar_3 bar_4 n3 n4

Diabetes comes last of these five, but it also feeds the first two, because it damages the blood vessels.
    draw bar_5 n5
---
